    karr list --status bogus      # header, "0 task(s)", exit 0
    karr list --priority bogus    # same
    karr list --class bogus       # "Usage error: unknown class ... (valid: ...)", exit 2  (k235)

A typo in the filter looks exactly like an empty board, and an agent reading `0 task(s)` concludes there is nothing to do. `move` already validates the same value ("invalid status "bogus" (valid: backlog, todo, ...)", exit 2), `--class` got the same treatment in k235 and `--sort` validates too, so the rule and the wording exist; `--status` and `--priority` on list are the two filters that still skip it.

## What to build

Validate every element of the comma-separated `--status` and `--priority` lists against the board's config (statuses and priorities, plus `archived`) before filtering; refuse the unknown one with the existing "invalid status/priority ... (valid: ...)" line and exit 2. Same check for `pick --status` and `pick --move` if they lack it (verify first). Changes entry, tests.

Pointers: App::karr::Config validate_status and validate_priority (Cmd::Create calls them around line 200, Cmd::Move for the target status). Cmd::List validates --class in _validate_options (around line 384); --status and --priority go in the same place, element by element after the comma split. archived is a valid --status value although it is not one of the board's configured columns (Config->ARCHIVED_STATUS).

